winedmo: Use multi-threaded decoding for HEVC, VP9 and AV1 as well.

Proton-GE's winedmo backend (ge-video-rework 0076) enables libavcodec
threading for H.264 only; every other video codec keeps libavcodec's default
of one thread. High-resolution HEVC / VP9 / AV1 video then decodes on a single
core, while Valve's winegstreamer path decodes those codecs multi-threaded.
Apply the same bounded thread count to them.

Written for EX-Proton. Applies after Proton-GE's patch set.

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -921,7 +921,8 @@
             t->avctx->framerate.den = t->input_fps_den;
         }

-        if (codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264)
+        if (codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264 || codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC
+            || codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_VP9 || codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_AV1)
         {
             int thread_count = av_cpu_count();

